<title>USA: Greenspan Senate testimony set for July 23.</title>
<headline>Greenspan Senate testimony set for July 23.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan will deliver semi-annual Humphrey-Hawkins testimony to the Senate Banking Committee on July 23 at 10 a.m. EDT (1400 GMT), a spokesman for the committee said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The testimony will come one the day after Greenspan presents the same economic report to a House Banking subcommittee.</p>
<p>Also July 23, Fed Vice Chair Alice Rivlin will testify on the state of the economy to the House Banking Committee.</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsroom 202 898-8300))</p>
</text>
